cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its prediction archive, please cite it as below, and cite the
  pre-registration for the study design.
type: software
title: "Research-MaintAdapt-RUL: do remaining-useful-life leaderboards predict maintenance value?"
abstract: >-
  Companion repository of a pre-registered study that tests whether the accuracy metrics
  remaining-useful-life papers rank models by (RMSE and NASA score at the last observed cycle of
  the official C-MAPSS test engines) predict the maintenance value of the same models when their
  predictions drive a tuned maintenance alarm. It holds the cross-fitting pipeline, the decision
  layer, the confirmatory, secondary and exploratory analyses, the paper assets and an
  independent recomputation of the primary endpoints.
